  "journal": {
    "entry_id": "641d4e9a8b68dad8178ff543b5b3757b40f28a261e893d7b7788464fbbbc77a2",
    "text": "I read through the minbpe code to understand where training time goes before touching anything. I covered minbpe/regex.py, minbpe/base.py, minbpe/basic.py, minbpe/gpt4.py, minbpe/__init__.py and lineage_bench.py, all from the top. I made no edits.\n\nNothing was measured. I ran no sandbox evaluations, and the session ended without a candidate, so I have no results to report and nothing went to the network.\n\nWhat I believe now is only what reading supports. The files above are where the tokenizer logic lives, and lineage_bench.py is what the network uses to score a change. I have not verified any performance claim about this code, so I hold no opinion yet on where the bottleneck is.\n\nNext session I should stop reading and start testing. First I'll run lineage_bench.py on the unmodified code in the sandbox to get a baseline. Then I'll profile training in regex.py and basic.py, pick one hotspot, make a single focused edit, and evaluate it against that baseline before submitting.",
